[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186128713 :answer-field/choices 17592186128714] [:db/retract 17592186128713 :answer-field/choices 17592186128715] [:db/retract 17592186128713 :answer-field/choices 17592186128716] [:db/retract 17592186128713 :answer-field/choices 17592186128717] [:db/retract 17592186128713 :answer-field/choices 17592186128718] {:db/id 17592186129172 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-66ff7371-5323-5876-b071-49b4ca2a6463"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129872 :question/problem "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y,\\, & \\text{if}\\,0<x<2,\\,-1<y<0, \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y),\\, & \\text{if}\\,0<x<2,\\,0<y<1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{(0,2)\\times (-1,1)}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the rectangle $R$ can be represented as a union of two smaller rectangles, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =(0,2)\\times ((-1,0)\\cup (0,1)) \\\\  & =((0,2)\\times (-1,0))\\cup ((0,2)\\times (0,1)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{(0,2)\\times (-1,0)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(0,2)\\times (0,1)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{(0,2)\\times (-1,0)}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(0,2)\\times (0,1)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186128713 :answer-field/correct "answer-c5b9d0b8-9a3f-5bdc-b4d0-bb4eb57acfcf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5ba92148-b911-57fa-bcc8-d6592d9da4b9" "answer-48d84918-aaf4-5e48-802a-eb621ffae666" "answer-c5b9d0b8-9a3f-5bdc-b4d0-bb4eb57acfcf" "answer-822a278f-47f8-5535-9796-535bd9d05cea" "answer-34b43744-10b8-5bdd-86b0-6a7b66637027"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ba92148-b911-57fa-bcc8-d6592d9da4b9" :answer/id #uuid "5ba92148-b911-57fa-bcc8-d6592d9da4b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{∬}_{(-1,1)}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(0,2)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48d84918-aaf4-5e48-802a-eb621ffae666" :answer/id #uuid "48d84918-aaf4-5e48-802a-eb621ffae666" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{∬}_{(0,1)\\times (-1,1)}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (-1,1)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5b9d0b8-9a3f-5bdc-b4d0-bb4eb57acfcf" :answer/id #uuid "c5b9d0b8-9a3f-5bdc-b4d0-bb4eb57acfcf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{∬}_{(0,2)\\times (-1,0)}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(0,2)\\times (0,1)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-822a278f-47f8-5535-9796-535bd9d05cea" :answer/id #uuid "822a278f-47f8-5535-9796-535bd9d05cea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{∬}_{(0,2)\\times (-1,1)}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(0,2)\\times (-1,1)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-34b43744-10b8-5bdd-86b0-6a7b66637027" :answer/id #uuid "34b43744-10b8-5bdd-86b0-6a7b66637027" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{∬}_{(0,2)}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(-1,1)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-66ff7371-5323-5876-b071-49b4ca2a6463" :question/id #uuid "66ff7371-5323-5876-b071-49b4ca2a6463" :question/math-academy-id "q-80674" :question/problem "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y),\\, & \\text{if}\\,0<x<\\pi ,\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<y<0, \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y),\\, & \\text{if}\\,0<x<\\pi ,\\,0<y<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (-\\pi /2,\\pi /2)}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the rectangle $R$ can be represented as a union of two smaller rectangles, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =(0,\\pi )\\times ((-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0)\\cup (0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =((0,\\pi )\\times (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0))\\cup ((0,\\pi )\\times (0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (-\\pi /2,0)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (0,\\pi /2)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (-\\pi /2,0)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (0,\\pi /2)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c22f973c-4187-5d34-928b-a206bc95c78a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c22f973c-4187-5d34-928b-a206bc95c78a" :answer-field/id #uuid "c22f973c-4187-5d34-928b-a206bc95c78a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ff3ec6df-aa0b-5131-ba4c-022b02da3f60" :answer-field/choices ["answer-27dab55e-2a07-5559-adf9-474a787ae042" "answer-ff3ec6df-aa0b-5131-ba4c-022b02da3f60" "answer-db274e58-8e5f-5077-88fc-c9024b1f6057" "answer-4a503419-3b03-55f7-a026-c71a3cdf1fda" "answer-cf8aa907-71bd-57bd-b9b0-a791585844c8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27dab55e-2a07-5559-adf9-474a787ae042" :answer/id #uuid "27dab55e-2a07-5559-adf9-474a787ae042" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (-\\pi /2,0)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (0,\\pi /2)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-y)\\,\\text{d}A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff3ec6df-aa0b-5131-ba4c-022b02da3f60" :answer/id #uuid "ff3ec6df-aa0b-5131-ba4c-022b02da3f60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (-\\pi /2,0)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (0,\\pi /2)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)\\,\\text{d}A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db274e58-8e5f-5077-88fc-c9024b1f6057" :answer/id #uuid "db274e58-8e5f-5077-88fc-c9024b1f6057" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (-\\pi /2,0)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)\\,\\text{d}A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a503419-3b03-55f7-a026-c71a3cdf1fda" :answer/id #uuid "4a503419-3b03-55f7-a026-c71a3cdf1fda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (-\\pi /2,0)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (0,\\pi /2)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf8aa907-71bd-57bd-b9b0-a791585844c8" :answer/id #uuid "cf8aa907-71bd-57bd-b9b0-a791585844c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (-\\pi /2,\\pi /2)}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y))\\text{ }\\text{d}A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129188 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1d37bcc4-0c9f-508d-8122-95d6a1703d93"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-1d37bcc4-0c9f-508d-8122-95d6a1703d93" :question/id #uuid "1d37bcc4-0c9f-508d-8122-95d6a1703d93" :question/math-academy-id "q-130018" :question/problem "Given that $C$ and $D$ are finite, non-overlapping regions and that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=-5,\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=-10,\n$$\n\nfind the value of \n\n$$\n{∬}_{C\\cup D}2f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity and additivity of double integrals, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{C\\cup D}2f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =2{∬}_{C\\cup D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A \\\\  & =2({∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A) \\\\  & =2(-5-10) \\\\  & =-30\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f08a4b5c-ff94-5bb7-9fc3-45c47e3170dd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f08a4b5c-ff94-5bb7-9fc3-45c47e3170dd" :answer-field/id #uuid "f08a4b5c-ff94-5bb7-9fc3-45c47e3170dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-